  "id": "ml-ai-170",
  "title": "dplyr Package in R Programming - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The dplyr package for R offers efficient data manipulation functions. It makes data transformation and summarization simple with concise, readable syntax.</span></p><h2 id=\"key-features-of-dplyr\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Key Features of dplyr</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Here are some important features of dplyr that make working with data easier.</span></p><h3 id=\"data-frame-and-tibble\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>1. Data Frame</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Data frames in dplyr in R is organized tables where each column stores specific types of information, like names, ages, or scores for creating a data frame involves specifying column names and their respective values.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">df</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">data.frame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"vipul\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"jayesh\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"anurag\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"n\">Age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">25</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">23</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">22</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Score</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">95</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">89</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">78</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"n\">df</span><span class=\"w\">                 </span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-1.webp\" alt=\"dplyr_\" width=\"200\" height=\"190\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624123100113138/dplyr_.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624123100113138/dplyr_-100.webp 100w\"><figcaption>A data.frame</figcaption></figure><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Note: T</strong></b><span>ibbles introduced through the </span><a href=\"#/article/ml-ai/ml-ai-706\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span>tibble package</span></a><span>, share similar functionality but offer enhanced user-friendly features. The syntax for creating a tibble is similar to that of a data frame.</span></p></blockquote><h3 id=\"pipes-\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>2. Pipes (</strong></b><b><code><strong>%&gt;%</strong></code></b><b><strong>)</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>dplyr in R The pipe operator (</span><code><span>%&gt;%</span></code><span>) in dplyr package, which allows us to chain multiple operations together, improving code readability. </span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"nf\">library</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dplyr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mtcars</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">filter</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mpg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">20</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span><span class=\"w\">\t </span>\n<span class=\"nf\">select</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mpg</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cyl</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"nf\">group_by</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cyl</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span><span class=\"w\">\t\t</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">summarise</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mean_hp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">mean</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">result</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-2.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-06-24-123750\" width=\"335\" height=\"197\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624123839268509/Screenshot-2025-06-24-123750.webp 335w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624123839268509/Screenshot-2025-06-24-123750-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624123839268509/Screenshot-2025-06-24-123750-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624123839268509/Screenshot-2025-06-24-123750-300.webp 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"important-dplyr-functions\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Important dplyr Functions</span></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>dplyr in R provides various important functions that can be used for Data Manipulation. These are:&nbsp;</span></p><h3 id=\"filter-function\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>1. filter()</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For choosing cases and using their values as a base for doing so.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">data.frame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Abhi\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Bhavesh\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Chaman\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Dimri\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">16</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">46</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">69</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">school</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">r_w_na</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">filter</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nf\">is.na</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r_w_na</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">r_w_na</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">filter</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"nf\">is.na</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r_w_na</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b><span>&nbsp;</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-3.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-06-24-124451\" width=\"203\" height=\"198\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624124540570280/Screenshot-2025-06-24-124451.webp 203w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624124540570280/Screenshot-2025-06-24-124451-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624124540570280/Screenshot-2025-06-24-124451-200.webp 200w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"arrange\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>2. arrange()</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For reordering of the cases.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">data.frame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Abhi\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Bhavesh\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Chaman\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Dimri\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">16</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">46</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">69</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"n\">school</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">d.name</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">arrange</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d.name</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b><span>&nbsp;</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-4.webp\" alt=\"image\" width=\"213\" height=\"182\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624155759537016/image.webp 213w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624155759537016/image-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624155759537016/image-200.webp 200w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"select-and-rename\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>3. select() and rename()</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For choosing variables and using their names as a base for doing so.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"nf\">library</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dplyr</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">data.frame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Abhi\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Bhavesh\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Chaman\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Dimri\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">16</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">46</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">69</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">school</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">d_new</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nf\">select</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">contains</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"h\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%&gt;%</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nf\">rename</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d_new</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b><span>&nbsp;</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-5.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-06-24-144402\" width=\"285\" height=\"123\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624144800091369/Screenshot-2025-06-24-144402.webp 285w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624144800091369/Screenshot-2025-06-24-144402-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624144800091369/Screenshot-2025-06-24-144402-200.webp 200w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"4-mutate-and-transmute\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>4. mutate() and transmute()</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Addition of new variables which are the functions of prevailing variables.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">data.frame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Abhi\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Bhavesh\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Chaman\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Dimri\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">16</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">46</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">69</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">school</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">mutate</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">transmute</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b><span>&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>    </span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-6.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-06-24-130842\" width=\"343\" height=\"457\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624130922058799/Screenshot-2025-06-24-130842.webp 343w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624130922058799/Screenshot-2025-06-24-130842-100.webp 75w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624130922058799/Screenshot-2025-06-24-130842-200.webp 150w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624130922058799/Screenshot-2025-06-24-130842-300.webp 225w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"summarise\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>5. summarise()</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Condensing various values to one value.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">data.frame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Abhi\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Bhavesh\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Chaman\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Dimri\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">16</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">46</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">69</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">school</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">summarise</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">mean_age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">mean</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">na.rm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">TRUE</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">min_age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">min</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">na.rm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">TRUE</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">max_age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">max</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">na.rm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">TRUE</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"n\">median_age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">median</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">na.rm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">TRUE</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b><span>&nbsp;</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-7.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-06-24-145124\" width=\"398\" height=\"155\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624145210307279/Screenshot-2025-06-24-145124.webp 398w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624145210307279/Screenshot-2025-06-24-145124-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624145210307279/Screenshot-2025-06-24-145124-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624145210307279/Screenshot-2025-06-24-145124-300.webp 300w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"sample_n-and-sample_frac\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>6. sample_n() and sample_frac()</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>For taking random specimens.</span></p><gfg-tabs data-run-ide=\"false\" data-mode=\"light\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">R</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"r\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-r\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">data.frame</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"Abhi\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Bhavesh\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                          </span><span class=\"s\">\"Chaman\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Dimri\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"n\">age</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">7</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">9</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">16</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>\n<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"m\">46</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">NA</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">69</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                 </span><span class=\"n\">school</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">c</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"yes\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"no\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">sample_n</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">3</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">sample_frac</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"m\">0.50</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b><span>&nbsp;</span></p><figure class=\"image\"><img src=\"./images/ml-ai-170-img-8.webp\" alt=\"Screenshot-2025-06-24-131305\" width=\"266\" height=\"324\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624131335371392/Screenshot-2025-06-24-131305.webp 266w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624131335371392/Screenshot-2025-06-24-131305-100.webp 82w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250624131335371392/Screenshot-2025-06-24-131305-200.webp 164w\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure></div>",
  "textContent": "The dplyr package for R offers efficient data manipulation functions. It makes data transformation and summarization simple with concise, readable syntax.Key Features of dplyrHere are some important features of dplyr that make working with data easier.1. Data FrameData frames in dplyr in R is organized tables where each column stores specific types of information, like names, ages, or scores for creating a data frame involves specifying column names and their respective values.\n            R\n\n    df <- data.frame(Name = c(\"vipul\", \"jayesh\", \"anurag\"),\n                 Age = c(25, 23, 22), Score = c(95, 89, 78))\ndf                 \n\nOutput:A data.frameNote: Tibbles introduced through the tibble package, share similar functionality but offer enhanced user-friendly features. The syntax for creating a tibble is similar to that of a data frame.2. Pipes (%>%)dplyr in R The pipe operator (%>%) in dplyr package, which allows us to chain multiple operations together, improving code readability. \n            R\n\n    library(dplyr)\n\nresult <- mtcars %>%\nfilter(mpg > 20) %>%\t \nselect(mpg, cyl, hp) %>% \ngroup_by(cyl) %>%\t\t\nsummarise(mean_hp = mean(hp)) \n\nprint(result)\n\nOutput:OutputImportant dplyr Functionsdplyr in R provides various important functions that can be used for Data Manipulation. These are: 1. filter()For choosing cases and using their values as a base for doing so.\n            R\n\n    d <- data.frame(name = c(\"Abhi\", \"Bhavesh\", \"Chaman\", \"Dimri\"),\n                age = c(7, 5, 9, 16),\n                ht = c(46, NA, NA, 69),\n                school = c(\"yes\", \"yes\", \"no\", \"no\"))\n\nprint(d)\n\nr_w_na <- d %>% filter(is.na(ht))\nprint(r_w_na)\n\nr_w_na <- d %>% filter(!is.na(ht))\nprint(r_w_na)\n\nOutput: Output2. arrange()For reordering of the cases.\n            R\n\n    d <- data.frame( name = c(\"Abhi\", \"Bhavesh\", \"Chaman\", \"Dimri\"), \n                 age = c(7, 5, 9, 16), \n                 ht = c(46, NA, NA, 69),\n                 school = c(\"yes\", \"yes\", \"no\", \"no\") )\nprint(d)\n\nd.name<- arrange(d, age)\nprint(d.name)\n\nOutput: Output3. select() and rename()For choosing variables and using their names as a base for doing so.\n            R\n\n    library(dplyr)\n\nd <- data.frame(name=c(\"Abhi\", \"Bhavesh\", \"Chaman\", \"Dimri\"),\n                age=c(7, 5, 9, 16),\n                ht=c(46, NA, NA, 69),\n                school=c(\"yes\", \"yes\", \"no\", \"no\"))\n\nd_new <- d %>%\n  select(name, age, contains(\"h\")) %>%\n  rename(height = ht)\n\nprint(d_new)\n\nOutput: Output4. mutate() and transmute()Addition of new variables which are the functions of prevailing variables.\n            R\n\n    d <- data.frame(name = c(\"Abhi\", \"Bhavesh\", \"Chaman\", \"Dimri\"), \n                age = c(7, 5, 9, 16), \n                ht = c(46, NA, NA, 69),\n                school = c(\"yes\", \"yes\", \"no\", \"no\"))\n\nmutate(d, x3 = ht + age)\n\ntransmute(d, x3 = ht + age)\n\nOutput:     Output5. summarise()Condensing various values to one value.\n            R\n\n    d <- data.frame(\n  name = c(\"Abhi\", \"Bhavesh\", \"Chaman\", \"Dimri\"),\n  age = c(7, 5, 9, 16),\n  ht = c(46, NA, NA, 69),\n  school = c(\"yes\", \"yes\", \"no\", \"no\")\n)\n\nsummarise(d, \n          mean_age = mean(age, na.rm = TRUE), \n          min_age = min(age, na.rm = TRUE), \n          max_age = max(age, na.rm = TRUE), \n          median_age = median(age, na.rm = TRUE))\n\nOutput: Output6. sample_n() and sample_frac()For taking random specimens.\n            R\n\n    d <- data.frame( name = c(\"Abhi\", \"Bhavesh\",\n                          \"Chaman\", \"Dimri\"), \n                 age = c(7, 5, 9, 16), \n                 ht = c(46, NA, NA, 69),\n                 school = c(\"yes\", \"yes\", \"no\", \"no\") )\n\nsample_n(d, 3)\n\nsample_frac(d, 0.50)\n\nOutput: Output",
  "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/r-language/dplyr-package-in-r-programming"
}
